<div id="mailSetupGuide" class="pd-overlay hidden mail-setup-guide" data-portal-dialog data-managed-dialog role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="mailSetupGuideTitle"><div class="pd-card"><header class="pd-header"><div class="pd-heading-copy"><p class="ot-eyebrow">MAIL SERVER SETTINGS</p><h2 id="mailSetupGuideTitle">Email setup guide</h2><p>Set the account that sends updates from the Guidance Office.</p></div><button type="button" class="pd-close" id="mailSetupGuideClose" aria-label="Close email setup guide" onclick="window.PortalDialogs.close(document.getElementById('mailSetupGuide'))">×</button></header><div class="pd-body">
<h3>1. Get the school's approved sending account</h3><p>Ask your school IT administrator or email provider for the SMTP server, port, encryption and approved login method. Use an account the Guidance Office is authorized to send from.</p>
<h3>2. Fill in the mail settings</h3><table data-cw-no-cards aria-label="Mail settings fields"><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>What to enter</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>SMTP server</td><td>The outgoing server supplied by the email provider.</td></tr><tr><td>Port and encryption</td><td>Use the matching pair supplied by your provider. Gmail supports <strong>587 + STARTTLS</strong> or <strong>465 + SSL / TLS</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>Mail account</td><td>The full email address used to sign in to the sending account.</td></tr><tr><td>App password</td><td>The provider-approved app password or SMTP credential. Leaving this field blank keeps the saved credential. Enter a new one when changing the sending account.</td></tr><tr><td>Sender email</td><td>The sending account or an alias your provider has approved.</td></tr><tr><td>Sender name</td><td>The name recipients see, such as SRCB Guidance Office.</td></tr><tr><td>Enable email delivery</td><td>Turn this on when the settings are ready, then choose <strong>Save email settings</strong>.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>3. Gmail / Google Workspace example</h3><p>Use <strong>smtp.gmail.com</strong>, port <strong>587</strong> and <strong>STARTTLS</strong>, with the full sending email address. Where your Google account permits app passwords, turn on 2-Step Verification and create an app password for this website. Your school administrator may restrict this option. Changing the Google account password revokes existing app passwords; create and save a replacement when needed.</p><p class="ot-help">Follow <a href="https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/185833?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's official app-password instructions</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/mail/answer/7104828?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gmail's official SMTP settings</a>. If the provider requires OAuth or a managed relay, ask IT to confirm a supported setup before changing these fields.</p>
<h3>4. Check delivery</h3><ol><li>Save the settings and check that the page says <strong>Email configured</strong>.</li><li>Use an authorized test account to perform a normal action, such as submitting an exam application.</li><li>Watch <strong>Waiting</strong>, <strong>Sending</strong> and <strong>Sent</strong>. The background worker checks the queue every minute while the local Windows job and XAMPP are running.</li><li>Check the recipient's inbox and Spam/Junk folder. If <strong>Needs attention</strong> increases, verify the server details, credential and provider restrictions with IT.</li></ol><p>When hosted online, set the public website address in the website-address section and configure the appointment and email workers as server jobs. Previously delivered emails retain their original links.</p>
</div><footer class="pd-footer"><button type="button" class="pd-button primary" onclick="window.PortalDialogs.close(document.getElementById('mailSetupGuide'))">Got it</button></footer></div></div>
